{
  "inShort": "The checkpoint is at risk: no public build establishes the playable jump or first level. The devlog reports two successful playthroughs, but its image and video do not show the game. With one sprint left, access to the playable prototype remains unverified.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hf200z5xoz8qjmdfvfi",
      "text": "The public repository of Godot demo projects matches the task. It provides starting examples, not evidence of this game's jump or level."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hff00z6xoz88svm5zwp",
      "text": "The animated reference video's title and thumbnail establish a cartoon visual reference. The animation was not inspected, so that part remains unverified. The task stays done."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hfy00z7xoz83i3lhw8g",
      "text": "The playtesting reference article matches the task. It explains playtesting, but does not establish that this game's reported test occurred."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hgm00z9xoz8wh9h1eua",
      "text": "Cutting the trailer storyboard removes work that does not establish the playable jump or accessible first level."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The devlog reports that two friends reached the flag, with one falling into the second pit four times. This identifies a possible jump-difficulty issue, but no build or gameplay artifact supports the report.",
    "The image caption describes a jumping gnome, but the image shows mountains. The linked video's title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny, not the prototype; the video itself was not watched."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What playable build supports the reported playthroughs, and can someone outside the team open it?",
    "Does the second pit test the intended jump difficulty, or expose a control problem?",
    "Can the remaining scope stay at one short level with the jump, flag and launch instructions?"
  ],
  "direction": {
    "goal": {
      "value": "stalled",
      "why": "The playtest report adds a claim, but no accessible artifact newly establishes the playable jump or first level."
    },
    "stage": {
      "value": "stalled",
      "why": "The prototype-devlog requirement is already complete, but this sprint adds no inspectable evidence of the working core or chosen style."
    }
  },
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #3 reported successful playthroughs and a difficult pit; it received 0 applause and 0 views, and the project lists no store page or game link.",
    "team": "Only 10–15 stated hours remain, so Mia's two weeks without work confirmation leave engineering capacity beyond Alex unconfirmed. Across two sprints, the public evidence has not advanced toward the playable goal.",
    "management": "No planned tasks remain open, yet their completed artifacts do not close the checkpoint goal; the stage's sole required task is already satisfied. With 10–15 hours left, keep the scope to the claimed first level and publish an openable build with launch instructions, rather than adding content."
  }
}

